       ],
       "r": 3,
       "color": "blue"
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "at": [
        39.5,
        14
       ],
       "text": {
        "en": "Na⁺"
       },
       "size": 3,
       "color": "blue"
      },
      {
       "kind": "circle",
       "at": [
        54,
        20
       ],
       "r": 3,
       "color": "green"
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "at": [
        52,
        18
       ],
       "text": {
        "en": "Cl⁻"
       },
       "size": 3,
       "color": "green"
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "at": [
        61,
        16
       ],
       "text": {
        "en": "1 unit → 2 particles"
       },
       "size": 3,
       "color": "yellow"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "i compares what we observe with what we expect for no dissociation or association."
     },
     "draw": [
      {
       "kind": "math",
       "at": [
        4,
        28
       ],
       "tex": "i = \\frac{\\text{observed colligative property}}{\\text{calculated value}}",
       "size": 3,
       "color": "white"
      },
      {
       "kind": "math",
       "at": [
        4,
        40
       ],
       "tex": "i = \\frac{\\text{normal molar mass}}{\\text{abnormal molar mass}}",
       "size": 3,
       "color": "white"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Every colligative formula gets i in front."
     },
     "draw": [
      {
       "kind": "math",
       "at": [
        4,
        51
       ],
       "tex": "\\Delta T_f = i\\,K_f\\,m",
       "size": 4,
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "kind": "math",
       "at": [
        56,
        51
       ],
       "tex": "\\pi = i\\,CRT",
       "size": 4,
       "color": "yellow"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "For dissociation into n ions, alpha is i minus one over n minus one. Ethanoic acid in benzene dimerises, so i is less than one."
     },
     "draw": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "at": [
        4,
        2
       ],
       "text": {
        "en": "Degree of dissociation / association"
       },
       "size": 4,
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "kind": "math",
       "at": [
        4,
        11
       ],
       "tex": "\\alpha_{diss} = \\frac{i-1}{n-1}",
       "size": 4,
       "color": "green"
      },
      {
       "kind": "math",
       "at": [
        52,
        11
       ],
       "tex": "\\alpha_{assoc} = \\frac{1-i}{1-1/n}",
       "size": 4,
       "color": "orange"
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "at": [
        4,
        25
       ],
       "text": {
        "en": "Dissociation: i > 1"
       },
       "size": 3,
       "color": "green"
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "at": [
        52,
        25
       ],
       "text": {
        "en": "Association: i < 1"
       },
       "size": 3,
       "color": "orange"
      }
     ],
     "clear": true
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Example: 0.1 molal K2SO4, fully dissociated, gives three ions. Delta T f is 3 times 1.86 times 0.1, that is 0.558 K."
     },
     "draw": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "at": [
        4,
